  "facts": [
    "Grand Duchess Charlotte Bridge, unveiled in 1966, survived a daring overload test when twelve 42‑ton M48 Patton tanks crossed its deck, proving its strength before opening to traffic.",
    "Renovated from 2015‑2018, the bridge’s 26.58‑meter deck now hosts two tram lanes, two traffic lanes each direction, and a 3.69‑meter pedestrian‑bike path, all illuminated by sleek LED strips.",
    "Its striking red paint, chosen to stand out in fog, earned the nickname “Red Bridge,” a moniker that LuxTram cemented by naming its tram stop “Rout Bréck – Pafendal.”"
